-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- closed form where the roots are rational
-- Where every root of every m is one of given rationals r = 2^{e2} 3^{e3} (or 0), a root sum is a combination of
-- the radicals 2^{i/8} 3^{j/8}, 0 ≤ i, j < 8, which are linearly independent over the rationals; its coefficients
-- are the canonical exact value. A candidate root: the value and its exponents of 2 and 3.
Cand : Type
Cand = SQ × (Nat × Nat)
